<title>SWITZERLAND: Thieves steal hand grenades from Swiss armoury.</title>
<headline>Thieves steal hand grenades from Swiss armoury.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unidentified thieves broke into a Swiss army munitions depot and made off with 448 hand grenades, police in the western canton of Valais said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The thieves made a hole in a fence, removed a grille from a window and severed an iron bar to gain access to the explosive practice grenades in the Tuesday night break-in at the base in Bramois.</p>
<p>Practice grenades blow up but do not spray shrapnel.</p>
</text>
